{"chunk_id": "7057275f21ca", "text": "Dushmanta questions how Sakuntala could be the daughter of the austere sage Kanwa, since such ascetics are believed incapable of moral lapse. Sakuntala recounts what Kanwa once explained: the origin of her birth lies with the great sage Viswamitra. When Viswamitra\u2019s terrifying penances threatened Indra\u2019s throne, the king of the gods sent the celestial nymph Menaka to seduce him and break his austerities. Menaka hesitates, describing Viswamitra\u2019s immense spiritual power and wrath, but agrees after Indra arranges help from the wind-god and the god of love. At the hermitage, a staged gust steals Menaka\u2019s garments, exposing her before the meditating sage. Viswamitra succumbs to desire, and they live together for a time, conceiving a daughter\u2014Sakuntala. Menaka later abandons the infant by the Malini river, where birds guard the child until she is eventually found.\nSakuntala recounts how Indra sent the apsara Menaka to seduce the ascetic Viswamitra, leading to Sakuntala\u2019s birth and abandonment by the Malini river.\nThemes: divine interference, ascetic temptation, birth of Sakuntala, power of penance, celestial politics", "vector": [0.019696597009897232, -0.010180416516959667, 0.020265942439436913, 0.010146526619791985, -0.022868657484650612, 0.02547137439250946, -0.018327459692955017, -0.011671556159853935, -0.011644444428384304, -0.030093906447291374, 0.022665319964289665, 0.007842038758099079, 0.020415056496858597, 0.011759668588638306, -0.007875927723944187, 0.00514104263857007, 0.05284056439995766, 0.0028043589554727077, 0.018110567703843117, -0.019235700368881226, -0.009733074344694614, -0.006394955329596996, 0.009787297807633877, 0.02356000430881977, -0.039393194019794464, 0.021499520167708397, 0.008119932375848293, -0.029307669028639793, -0.008153822273015976, -0.019398368895053864, -0.014084490947425365, -0.006300064735114574, 0.006622015032917261, -0.02681339904665947, -0.0199948251247406, -0.00